---
import Admin from "../../layouts/Admin.astro";
---

<Admin title="Help">
  <div class="prose help">
    <h1>Help</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short guides for the things people do most. If something here is wrong or
      missing, tell the website committee.
    </p>

    <nav aria-label="On this page">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="#post">Post news or an event</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#approve">Approve something someone else wrote</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#schedule">
            Publish later, or take something down automatically
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#document">Add a form or document</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#page">Change the words on a page</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#facts">Change a phone number, fee or office hours</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#roster">Add or remove a board member</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#minutes">Write, approve and file minutes</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#accounts">Give someone access to this app</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="#site">When does the website update?</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="post">Post news or an event</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Go to <a href="/content/news/">News</a> (or{" "}
        <a href="/content/events/">Events</a>) and choose <strong>New</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fill in the title and summary. Write the full text in plain sentences;
        leave a blank line between paragraphs.
      </li>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>Save as draft</strong>. Nothing is public yet.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you see <strong>Publish</strong>, choose it and you are done. If you
        see <strong>Submit for approval</strong>, choose that; an admin, the
        secretary or a board member will publish it.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="approve">Approve something someone else wrote</h2>
    <p>
      Items waiting for approval appear at the top of <a href="/">Home</a>. Open
      one, read it, then choose <strong>Approve and publish</strong>, or{" "}
      <strong>Send back with a note</strong> saying what to change. You cannot
      approve something you submitted yourself.
    </p>

    <h2 id="schedule">Publish later, or take something down automatically</h2>
    <p>
      Every item has a <strong>Publish date</strong> in the panel beside it. Set
      a future date and time, then publish: it stays hidden until then. Set{" "}
      <strong>Hide after</strong> for a notice with a deadline, and choose
      whether to keep it here or delete it when the date passes.
    </p>

    <h2 id="document">Add a form or document</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Go to <a href="/content/documents/">Documents</a>, choose{" "}
        <strong>New</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>Choose the file (PDF, JPEG or PNG). It uploads straight away.</li>
      <li>
        Give it a title people will recognise, one sentence about what it is,
        and the section of the library it belongs in.
      </li>
      <li>Save, then publish or submit for approval.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      To replace a file, open the document, choose a new file, and save. The web
      address stays the same.
    </p>

    <h2 id="page">Change the words on a page</h2>
    <p>
      Go to <a href="/content/pages/">Pages</a> and open the page. The text is
      plain writing. For headings start a line with <code>## </code>; for a
      bullet start it with <code>- </code>. To mention the office email or phone
      write <code>{"{{email:general}}"}</code> or{" "}
      <code>{"{{phone:office}}"}</code> so the page never goes out of date.
    </p>

    <h2 id="facts">Change a phone number, fee or office hours</h2>
    <p>
      Facts that appear in more than one place live under{" "}
      <a href="/settings/">Site settings</a> (administrators only). Change a
      value once and every page that shows it changes.
    </p>

    <h2 id="roster">Add or remove a board member</h2>
    <p>
      Go to <a href="/roster/">Roster</a>. <strong>Add a person</strong> with
      their office and committees. When someone leaves, choose{" "}
      <strong>End term</strong>: they stop appearing as serving, but every
      record that names them is kept. The board page, committees page and the
      attendance list in minutes all come from the roster.
    </p>

    <h2 id="minutes">Write, approve and file minutes</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open the meeting under <a href="/meetings/">Meetings</a> and choose{" "}
        <strong>Minutes for this meeting</strong>, then{" "}
        <strong>Start minutes from the agenda</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Tick who was present. Write what was discussed under each item, and add
        motions with who moved and seconded them.
      </li>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>Save a new version</strong> as you go, then{" "}
        <strong>Send for review</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Board members read, comment, and mark the version reviewed. Fix anything
        raised and save again.
      </li>
      <li>
        Before the next meeting choose <strong>Ready for a vote</strong>. At the
        meeting, record the vote.
      </li>
      <li>
        Choose <strong>Export PDF</strong>, save it, upload it to PayHOA, then{" "}
        <strong>Mark as uploaded to PayHOA</strong>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Minutes are never on the public website; residents read them in PayHOA.
    </p>

    <h2 id="accounts">Give someone access to this app</h2>
    <p>
      Administrators go to <a href="/people/">Accounts</a> and invite the person
      with the email address of their Google account. They then sign in with
      Google. Roles decide what they can do: <em>editor</em> writes,{" "}
      <em>board</em> reviews and approves, <em>secretary</em> runs meetings and
      minutes, <em>admin</em> manages accounts and settings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="site">When does the website update?</h2>
    <p>
      Publishing here asks the website to rebuild, which takes a few minutes.
      The site also rebuilds every morning, which is when scheduled posts appear
      and expired ones disappear.
    </p>
  </div>
</Admin>
